module

public import Theory.SpecificGroups.Janko4.Model.AutomorphismReduction.FixedGenerator.NormalizerSquares.LocalAction.TwoCoreNormalizer.LinearModel
public import Theory.SpecificGroups.Janko4.Model.AutomorphismReduction.FixedGenerator.NormalizerSquares.LocalAction.TwoCoreNormalizer.LinearNormalizer.Reduction
public import Theory.SpecificGroups.Janko4.Model.AutomorphismReduction.FixedGenerator.NormalizerSquares.LocalAction.TwoCoreNormalizer.LinearNormalizer.CoreRecognition
public import Theory.SpecificGroups.Janko4.Model.AutomorphismReduction.FixedGenerator.NormalizerSquares.LocalAction.TwoCoreNormalizer.LinearNormalizer.QuotientCoverage

/-!
# Normalizer of the explicit binary local model

`actionGroup_selfNormalizer` proves that the literal subgroup generated by
the two certified binary matrices is self-normalizing in GL₁₂(2).

`CoreRecognition` proves that its actual derived subgroup is perfect and
constructs an equivalence of its central quotient with the concrete M₂₂.
`QuotientCoverage` then shows that the generated matrix group realizes every
automorphism of that quotient. Given a normalizing matrix, `Reduction` uses
perfectness to match its action on the core with conjugation by a group member.
Their quotient centralizes the core, so the certified matrix-centralizer
bound in `Centralizer` puts the original matrix in the generated group.

This is an intrinsic calculation for the specified matrices. Its intended
application to the J₄ local quotient action is motivated by GLS3, Table 5.3i,
printed p.270 (`refs/KGroup/GLS3/Chapter5(sec3-).tex`); the comparison with that
action is a separate theorem. The ATLAS matrices, attribution and source hashes
are retained in `LinearModel/source/`. The commutant and projective witnesses
are retained in `LinearNormalizer/source/` and
`LinearNormalizer/CoreRecognition/source/`.
-/

public section

namespace Janko4.OuterReduction.FixedGenerator.NormalizerSquares.TwoCoreLinearModel

/-- The literal binary matrix group realizes every automorphism of its core's
central quotient. -/
theorem derivedQuotientConjugation_surjective :
    Function.Surjective derivedQuotientConjugation :=
  derivedQuotientConjugation_surjective_of_equiv
    derivedGroup_eq_closure derivedQuotientEquivM22

/-- The subgroup generated by the two certified matrices is self-normalizing
in the full group of binary matrix units. -/
theorem actionGroup_selfNormalizer :
    Subgroup.normalizer (actionGroup : Set Matrix12ˣ) ≤ actionGroup :=
  actionGroup_selfNormalizer_of_perfect_quotient_coverage
    derivedQuotientConjugation_surjective

end Janko4.OuterReduction.FixedGenerator.NormalizerSquares.TwoCoreLinearModel
